    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "wait i see what u mean about the resource arn. i tried adding /* to the end of the bucket name but it still didnt work. id say the ARN looks like this now: arn:aws:s3:::my-app-logs-bucket/*\n\nis it possible the bucket itself is blocking it? i checked the bucket policy too and it looks fine. any idea what else could be causing an access denied error when i'm so sure the permissions are there?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If both the IAM policy and the bucket policy seem correct, the issue could stem from bucket-level configurations like Block Public Access settings, which can override permissions. Also, confirm that the region your Lambda is running in matches the region where the S3 bucket resides. Finally, a service control policy (SCP) applied at the AWS Organization level could be restricting access before your specific policies are even checked.",
      "source": "target",
